## Research Report: NuttX I2C Bus Driver Pattern and RK3506 I2C Controller

### 1. NuttX `i2c_master_s` Interface Structure and Callbacks

**Source:** `/home/b4qaq/project/openvela/nuttx/include/nuttx/i2c/i2c_master.h`

#### Core Structures

```c
/* The I2C vtable -- all callbacks a driver must implement */
struct i2c_ops_s
{
  CODE int (*transfer)(FAR struct i2c_master_s *dev,
                       FAR struct i2c_msg_s *msgs, int count);
#ifdef CONFIG_I2C_RESET
  CODE int (*reset)(FAR struct i2c_master_s *dev);
#endif
  CODE int (*setup)(FAR struct i2c_master_s *dev);
  CODE int (*shutdown)(FAR struct i2c_master_s *dev);
};

/* The base "class" -- every I2C driver embeds this as its first member */
struct i2c_master_s
{
  FAR const struct i2c_ops_s *ops;
};

/* A single I2C transaction segment (START to STOP or repeated-start) */
struct i2c_msg_s
{
  uint32_t frequency;         /* I2C frequency for this message */
  uint16_t addr;              /* Slave address (7- or 10-bit) */
  uint16_t flags;             /* I2C_M_READ, I2C_M_NOSTOP, I2C_M_NOSTART, etc. */
  FAR uint8_t *buffer;        /* Buffer to be transferred */
  ssize_t length;             /* Length of the buffer in bytes */
};
```

#### Key Macros (used by upper-half code and applications)

| Macro | Expansion | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `I2C_TRANSFER(d,m,c)` | `(d)->ops->transfer(d,m,c)` | Execute a sequence of I2C messages |
| `I2C_RESET(d)` | `(d)->ops->reset(d)` | Bus recovery (clock 9 cycles + STOP) |
| `I2C_SETUP(d)` | `(d)->ops->setup(d)` | Initialize the hardware |
| `I2C_SHUTDOWN(d)` | `(d)->ops->shutdown(d)` | Deinitialize the hardware |
| `I2C_ADDR8(a)` | `((a) << 1)` | Convert 7-bit to 8-bit R/W address |

#### Message Flags

| Flag | Value | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `I2C_M_READ` | `0x0001` | Read data (slave to master) |
| `I2C_M_TEN` | `0x0002` | Ten-bit address mode |
| `I2C_M_NOSTOP` | `0x0040` | No STOP at end of message (for repeated-start) |
| `I2C_M_NOSTART` | `0x0080` | No START at beginning (continuation) |

#### Public Helper Functions

```c
int i2c_register(FAR struct i2c_master_s *i2c, int bus);  /* Register as /dev/i2cN */
int i2c_writeread(dev, config, wbuffer, wbuflen, rbuffer, rbuflen);
int i2c_write(dev, config, buffer, buflen);
int i2c_read(dev, config, buffer, buflen);
```

